# Cosmos Data Factory — Curation and Retrieval
# Product / repo: cdf-curation-and-retrieval
#
# Three Docker images (glue only). Copy to .env for local overrides.
# This repo PULLS images; it does NOT build them.
#
# GA image registry/tag defaults live in ONE place: the root Makefile.
# Only set vars below to override locally (.env / local.env).
#
# One backbone (Curator + CDS HTTP + TAO).
# CDS public vs internal = runtime profile (image pin), not a second branch.
# See Makefile pull-* targets and README.md.

# ----- NGC image pins (optional overrides) -----
# Defaults: Makefile (COSMOS_CURATOR_*, DATASET_SEARCH_*, DATA_MINING_*)
# COSMOS_CURATOR_REGISTRY=...
# COSMOS_CURATOR_TAG=...
# COSMOS_CURATOR_IMAGE=...
# DATASET_SEARCH_REGISTRY=...
# DATASET_SEARCH_TAG=...
# DATASET_SEARCH_IMAGE=...
# DATA_MINING_REGISTRY=...
# DATA_MINING_TAG=...
# DATA_MINING_IMAGE=...
# COSMOS_EMBED_IMAGE=nvcr.io/nvidia/blueprint/cosmos-embed1-oss:1.2.0
# CDS_POSTGRES_IMAGE=<from the entitled repo>
# CAPTION_EMBED_NIM_IMAGE=<from the entitled repo>
# CRADIO_NIM_IMAGE=<from the entitled repo>

# ----- Dataset Search / CDS runtime profile -----
# public     = NGC blueprint (OSS default) — everyone
# internal   = entitled CDS, approved customers (do not commit private pins)
CDS_PROFILE=public

# Public profile (CDS 1.2.0):
#   make up-dataset-search adds deploy/compose/docker-compose.embed.yml, which
#   runs Cosmos-Embed1 as a service. From 1.2.0 the backend reads
#   COSMOS_EMBED_URI; without it the search pipeline never initialises and
#   collection calls return HTTP 500 "No pipelines have been initialised".
#   The CE1 OSS image cannot download weights
#   (COSMOS_EMBED_ALLOW_HF_DOWNLOAD=false), so COSMOS_EMBED_MODELS_DIR must
#   point at a Cosmos-Embed1 snapshot directory holding config.json and the
#   model-*.safetensors shards:
#     make pull-dataset-search
#     make up-dataset-search COSMOS_EMBED_MODELS_DIR=/path/to/Cosmos-Embed1-224p
#   Host port stays 9000, so --cosmos-embed-url defaults keep working.

# COSMOS_EMBED_MODELS_DIR=
# COSMOS_EMBED_PORT=9000
# COSMOS_EMBED_GPUS=1

# Internal profile (approved customers):
#   Access is granted with your entitlement; use the entitled repository's
#   README for the current image registry/tag.
#   Put overrides in gitignored local.env — never commit private hosts:
#     CDS_PROFILE=internal
#     DATASET_SEARCH_REGISTRY=<from the entitled repo>
#     DATASET_SEARCH_TAG=<from the entitled repo>
#     DATASET_SEARCH_IMAGE=cosmos-dataset-search
#     CDS_IMAGE=cosmos-dataset-search
#     CDS_TAG=<same as DATASET_SEARCH_TAG>
#   Then: docker login <registry> && make pull-dataset-search
#   Or retag a local entitled image via LOCAL_CDS_SOURCE_* +
#   make tag-local-images
#   Set CDS_PUBLIC_HOST to a hostname the browser can reach (not localhost
#   if the API is called from another machine).
#   Do not pass CDS_PROFILE=public / DATASET_SEARCH_TAG=1.2.0 on this profile.
# CDS deployed elsewhere (cluster, shared lab host): deploy it from its own
#   repository, then set CDS_URL at that API and run make ds-health.
#   Compose remains make up-dataset-search.

# Short aliases follow DATASET_SEARCH_* from the Makefile unless overridden:
# CDS_IMAGE=cosmos-dataset-search
# CDS_TAG=<same as DATASET_SEARCH_TAG>
CDS_URL=http://localhost:8888
# CDS_PUBLIC_HOST=localhost
# CDS_API_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:8888/v1

# Docker recipe defaults (make run-data-mining-select):
# GPUS=all
# DATA_MINING_SHM_SIZE=16g

# ----- Curator host sidecar (not a Docker image — host conda prefix) -----
FFMPEG_DIR=$(HOME)/cosmos-curator-ffmpeg
MODELS_DIR=$(HOME)/models

# ----- Optional Curator OpenAI-compatible HTTP endpoints -----
# These may point to any compatible service, such as vLLM or NIM.
# The selected cookbook controls which stages use remote endpoints.
#
# Role → Curator stage:
#   caption      window / event caption VLM
#   filter       VLM filter
#   classifier   video classifier
#   enhance      caption enhance LLM
#   embedding    remote embed API (optional; else local IV2)
#
# Configure endpoints in gitignored local.env:
# COSMOS_CURATOR_OPENAI_CAPTION_BASE_URL=https://caption-vlm.example.com/v1
# COSMOS_CURATOR_OPENAI_FILTER_BASE_URL=https://filter-vlm.example.com/v1
# COSMOS_CURATOR_OPENAI_CLASSIFIER_BASE_URL=https://classifier-vlm.example.com/v1
# COSMOS_CURATOR_OPENAI_ENHANCE_BASE_URL=https://enhance-llm.example.com/v1
# COSMOS_CURATOR_OPENAI_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=https://embedding.example.com/v1
#
# Supply API keys through a deployment secret manager or gitignored local.env.
# Never commit credential values.
# COSMOS_CURATOR_OPENAI_CAPTION_API_KEY=<provided-by-secret-manager>
# COSMOS_CURATOR_OPENAI_FILTER_API_KEY=<provided-by-secret-manager>
# COSMOS_CURATOR_OPENAI_CLASSIFIER_API_KEY=<provided-by-secret-manager>
# COSMOS_CURATOR_OPENAI_ENHANCE_API_KEY=<provided-by-secret-manager>
# COSMOS_CURATOR_OPENAI_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=<provided-by-secret-manager>
# HF_TOKEN=<provided-by-secret-manager>
